  "text": "A laser‑based sampling method combined with a high‑precision mass‑spectrometer was used to measure the ratios of a certain metal’s isotopes directly within tiny sections of tooth enamel, which grows in layers over time. By applying this technique to a large number of samples, the study compared isotopic patterns across different individuals and locations. These patterns reveal how people moved across the landscape, what areas they exploited for food, and the typical size of their groups. The findings also shed light on how distinct human communities interacted biologically and culturally, offering a clearer picture of past mobility and resource use."
